window.MOCK={"subj":"nss","stitle":"Networks, Signals & Systems","n":18,"title":"Fourier Series","marks":293,"qs":[{"i":1,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a rectangular pulse train (high for a fraction 0.4 of the period) of peak value 10. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L96.0 38.4L96.0 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L199.3 38.4L199.3 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$10$","$5$","$4$","$6.366$"],"a":2,"s":"$a_0=A\\,D=10\\times0.4=4$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":2,"q":"$x(t)=1+6\\cos\\omega_0t+3\\sin\\omega_0t+3\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$7$","$28$","$55$","$84.5$"],"a":1,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=1^2+\\dfrac{6^2+3^2}{2}+\\dfrac{3^2}{2}=28$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":3,"q":"$x(t)=2+10\\cos(3t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{1+j\\omega}$. Find the dc component of the output.","f":null,"o":["$12$","$4$","$1$","$2$"],"a":3,"s":"DC passes through $H(0)=1/1$: output dc $=2/1=2$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":4,"q":"$x(t)$ has period $T=4$ s and its coefficient $c_3$ is real and positive. What is $\\angle c_3$ for $y(t)=x(t-1)$ (in degrees, principal value)?","f":null,"o":["$-90^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$0^\\circ$","$540^\\circ$"],"a":1,"s":"Time shift: $c_k\\to c_ke^{-jk\\omega_0t_0}$; $\\omega_0=2\\pi/4$ ⇒ angle $=-3\\cdot90^\\circ\\cdot1=90^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":5,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±5 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_1$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">5</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-5</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$5$","$3.183$","$12.73$","$6.366$"],"a":3,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_1=\\dfrac{4(5)}{1\\pi}=6.366$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":6,"q":"Find $c_0$ of $x(t)=2+10\\cos(1t)+1\\sin(3t)$.","f":null,"o":["$12$","$1$","$2$","$5$"],"a":2,"s":"$c_0$ is the average value (DC term) $=2$; the sinusoids average to zero.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":7,"q":"The spectral lines of a periodic signal occur at …","f":null,"o":["frequencies $\\sqrt{k}\\,\\omega_0$","only at DC","integer multiples of the fundamental frequency","all real frequencies"],"a":2,"s":"Line spectrum at $k\\omega_0$.","m":1,"t":"Fourier series concepts"},{"i":8,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 4 and duty ratio 0.1 (pulse width $\\tau=0.1T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{4}|$, the magnitude of the 4th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L65.0 38.4L65.0 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L168.3 38.4L168.3 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$1.211$","$0.3183$","$0.3027$","$0.4$"],"a":2,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{4}{4\\pi}|\\sin(0.4\\pi)|=0.3027$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":9,"q":"$x(t)=2\\cos(2t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{3+j\\omega}$. Find the amplitude of the output.","f":null,"o":["$0.5547$","$0.6667$","$1$","$1.109$"],"a":0,"s":"Each harmonic is scaled by $H(jk\\omega_0)$: $|H(j2)|=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt{9+4}}=0.2774$ ⇒ amplitude $0.5547$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":10,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±2 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 1st. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$4$","$3.242$","$2$","$1.621$"],"a":1,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le1$: $3.242$ (total power $4$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":11,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)=2\\cos(5t+90^\\circ)$ has exponential Fourier series $\\sum c_ke^{jk\\omega_0t}$. Find $|c_1|$.","f":null,"o":["$0.5$","$1$","$1.414$","$2$"],"a":1,"s":"$\\cos(\\omega_0t+\\phi)=\\tfrac12e^{j\\phi}e^{j\\omega_0t}+\\tfrac12e^{-j\\phi}e^{-j\\omega_0t}$ ⇒ $c_1=\\dfrac{2}{2}e^{j90^\\circ}$: $|c_1|=1$, $\\angle c_1=90^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":12,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a full-wave rectified sine of peak value 4. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 93.9L65.0 83.9L70.2 74.3L75.3 65.5L80.5 57.6L85.7 50.9L90.8 45.5L96.0 41.6L101.2 39.2L106.3 38.4L111.5 39.2L116.7 41.6L121.8 45.5L127.0 50.9L132.2 57.6L137.3 65.5L142.5 74.3L147.7 83.9L152.8 93.9L158.0 104.2L163.2 93.9L168.3 83.9L173.5 74.3L178.7 65.5L183.8 57.6L189.0 50.9L194.2 45.5L199.3 41.6L204.5 39.2L209.7 38.4L214.8 39.2L220.0 41.6L225.2 45.5L230.3 50.9L235.5 57.6L240.7 65.5L245.8 74.3L251.0 83.9L256.2 93.9L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$4$","$1.273$","$2$","$2.546$"],"a":3,"s":"$a_0=2A/\\pi$. $=2.546$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":13,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=5$ and $b_n=12$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$. Find $\\angle c_n$ in degrees.","f":null,"o":["$67.38^\\circ$","$22.62^\\circ$","$157.4^\\circ$","$-67.38^\\circ$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{5-j12}{2}$ ⇒ $\\angle c_n=-\\tan^{-1}(b_n/a_n)=-67.38^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":14,"q":"The Gibbs phenomenon refers to …","f":null,"o":["the loss of the dc term","an overshoot of about 9 % near a discontinuity that does not vanish as more terms are added","aliasing of harmonics","non-convergence of the series at all points"],"a":1,"s":"Partial sums overshoot by ≈ 9 % of the jump; the width shrinks but the height stays.","m":1,"t":"Fourier series concepts"},{"i":15,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±5 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 3rd. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$12.5$","$25$","$22.52$","$20.26$"],"a":2,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le3$: $22.52$ (total power $25$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":16,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a sawtooth rising from 0 to A of peak value 3. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L158.0 38.4L158.0 104.2L261.3 38.4\"/></svg>","o":["$1.5$","$3$","$1.91$","$2.4$"],"a":0,"s":"Linear ramp from 0 to $A$: average $A/2$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":17,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=1$ and $b_n=1$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$ (so $x\\ni a_n\\cos n\\omega_0t+b_n\\sin n\\omega_0t$). Find $|c_n|$.","f":null,"o":["$1$","$0.3536$","$0.7071$","$1.414$"],"a":2,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{a_n-jb_n}{2}$ ⇒ $|c_n|=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{2}=0.7071$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":18,"q":"Find $c_0$ of $x(t)=2+2\\cos(1t)+3\\sin(3t)$.","f":null,"o":["$3$","$1$","$4$","$2$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_0$ is the average value (DC term) $=2$; the sinusoids average to zero.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":19,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=6$ and $b_n=8$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$ (so $x\\ni a_n\\cos n\\omega_0t+b_n\\sin n\\omega_0t$). Find $|c_n|$.","f":null,"o":["$2.5$","$5$","$10$","$7$"],"a":1,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{a_n-jb_n}{2}$ ⇒ $|c_n|=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{100}=5$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":20,"q":"$x(t)=3+4\\cos(4t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{3+j\\omega}$. Find the dc component of the output.","f":null,"o":["$1$","$3$","$9$","$0.3333$"],"a":0,"s":"DC passes through $H(0)=1/3$: output dc $=3/3=1$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":21,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 10 and duty ratio 0.2 (pulse width $\\tau=0.2T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{8}|$, the magnitude of the 8th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L75.3 38.4L75.3 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L178.7 38.4L178.7 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$2$","$0.3784$","$-3.027$","$0.3979$"],"a":1,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{10}{8\\pi}|\\sin(1.6\\pi)|=0.3784$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":22,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±5 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 5th. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$12.5$","$25$","$23.33$","$20.26$"],"a":2,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le5$: $23.33$ (total power $25$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":23,"q":"$x(t)$ has period $T=2$ s and its coefficient $c_4$ is real and positive. What is $\\angle c_4$ for $y(t)=x(t-0.25)$ (in degrees, principal value)?","f":null,"o":["$0^\\circ$","$360^\\circ$","$-180^\\circ$","$180^\\circ$"],"a":2,"s":"Time shift: $c_k\\to c_ke^{-jk\\omega_0t_0}$; $\\omega_0=2\\pi/2$ ⇒ angle $=-4\\cdot180^\\circ\\cdot0.25=-180^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":24,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=4$ and $b_n=3$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$ (so $x\\ni a_n\\cos n\\omega_0t+b_n\\sin n\\omega_0t$). Find $|c_n|$.","f":null,"o":["$1.25$","$5$","$2.5$","$3.5$"],"a":2,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{a_n-jb_n}{2}$ ⇒ $|c_n|=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{25}=2.5$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":25,"q":"If the period of a signal is doubled (same shape in each period, zero padding added), the spacing between spectral lines …","f":null,"o":["halves","stays the same","becomes zero","doubles"],"a":0,"s":"$\\omega_0=2\\pi/T$.","m":1,"t":"Fourier series concepts"},{"i":26,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot2\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot30\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$4$","$32$","$2$","$30$"],"a":2,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(2,30)=2$ Hz (period $0.5$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":27,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a full-wave rectified sine of peak value 10. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 93.9L65.0 83.9L70.2 74.3L75.3 65.5L80.5 57.6L85.7 50.9L90.8 45.5L96.0 41.6L101.2 39.2L106.3 38.4L111.5 39.2L116.7 41.6L121.8 45.5L127.0 50.9L132.2 57.6L137.3 65.5L142.5 74.3L147.7 83.9L152.8 93.9L158.0 104.2L163.2 93.9L168.3 83.9L173.5 74.3L178.7 65.5L183.8 57.6L189.0 50.9L194.2 45.5L199.3 41.6L204.5 39.2L209.7 38.4L214.8 39.2L220.0 41.6L225.2 45.5L230.3 50.9L235.5 57.6L240.7 65.5L245.8 74.3L251.0 83.9L256.2 93.9L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$3.183$","$5$","$6.366$","$10$"],"a":2,"s":"$a_0=2A/\\pi$. $=6.366$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":28,"q":"Find $c_0$ of $x(t)=1+2\\cos(10t)+2\\sin(30t)$.","f":null,"o":["$1$","$2$","$0.5$","$3$"],"a":0,"s":"$c_0$ is the average value (DC term) $=1$; the sinusoids average to zero.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":29,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 4 and duty ratio 0.1 (pulse width $\\tau=0.1T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{5}|$, the magnitude of the 5th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L65.0 38.4L65.0 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L168.3 38.4L168.3 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$0.2546$","$0.5093$","$1.273$","$0.4$"],"a":0,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{4}{5\\pi}|\\sin(0.5\\pi)|=0.2546$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":30,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±3 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 3rd. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$4.5$","$8.106$","$7.295$","$9$"],"a":1,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le3$: $8.106$ (total power $9$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":31,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±2 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_4$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-2</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$0.1592$","$0$","$2.546$","$0.3183$"],"a":1,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $n=4$ is even ⇒ $b_4=0$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":32,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 83.9L65.0 65.5L70.2 50.9L75.3 41.6L80.5 38.4L85.7 41.6L90.8 50.9L96.0 65.5L101.2 83.9L106.3 104.2L111.5 104.2L116.7 104.2L121.8 104.2L127.0 104.2L132.2 104.2L137.3 104.2L142.5 104.2L147.7 104.2L152.8 104.2L158.0 104.2L163.2 83.9L168.3 65.5L173.5 50.9L178.7 41.6L183.8 38.4L189.0 41.6L194.2 50.9L199.3 65.5L204.5 83.9L209.7 104.2L214.8 104.2L220.0 104.2L225.2 104.2L230.3 104.2L235.5 104.2L240.7 104.2L245.8 104.2L251.0 104.2L256.2 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["Only sine terms, odd harmonics only","A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)"],"a":1,"s":"Half-wave rectified sine contains dc, the fundamental sine, and even harmonics only (no odd harmonics except the fundamental).","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":33,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=10$ and $b_n=24$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$. Find $\\angle c_n$ in degrees.","f":null,"o":["$-67.38^\\circ$","$157.4^\\circ$","$22.62^\\circ$","$67.38^\\circ$"],"a":0,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{10-j24}{2}$ ⇒ $\\angle c_n=-\\tan^{-1}(b_n/a_n)=-67.38^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":34,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 83.9L65.0 65.5L70.2 50.9L75.3 41.6L80.5 38.4L85.7 41.6L90.8 50.9L96.0 65.5L101.2 83.9L106.3 104.2L111.5 104.2L116.7 104.2L121.8 104.2L127.0 104.2L132.2 104.2L137.3 104.2L142.5 104.2L147.7 104.2L152.8 104.2L158.0 104.2L163.2 83.9L168.3 65.5L173.5 50.9L178.7 41.6L183.8 38.4L189.0 41.6L194.2 50.9L199.3 65.5L204.5 83.9L209.7 104.2L214.8 104.2L220.0 104.2L225.2 104.2L230.3 104.2L235.5 104.2L240.7 104.2L245.8 104.2L251.0 104.2L256.2 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms","Only sine terms, odd harmonics only","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)"],"a":1,"s":"Half-wave rectified sine contains dc, the fundamental sine, and even harmonics only (no odd harmonics except the fundamental).","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":35,"q":"$x(t)=4\\cos(4t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{2+j\\omega}$. Find the amplitude of the output.","f":null,"o":["$0.8944$","$1$","$2$","$1.789$"],"a":0,"s":"Each harmonic is scaled by $H(jk\\omega_0)$: $|H(j4)|=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt{4+16}}=0.2236$ ⇒ amplitude $0.8944$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":36,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±1 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_9$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">1</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-1</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$0.01572$","$1.273$","$0.1415$","$0.07074$"],"a":2,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_9=\\dfrac{4(1)}{9\\pi}=0.1415$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":37,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 1 and duty ratio 0.25 (pulse width $\\tau=0.25T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{4}|$, the magnitude of the 4th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">1</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L80.5 38.4L80.5 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L183.8 38.4L183.8 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$0.07958$","$1$","$0.25$","$0$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{1}{4\\pi}|\\sin(1\\pi)|=0$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":38,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 1 and duty ratio 0.5 (pulse width $\\tau=0.5T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{4}|$, the magnitude of the 4th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">1</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L106.3 38.4L106.3 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L209.7 38.4L209.7 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$0$","$0.5$","$1$","$0.07958$"],"a":0,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{1}{4\\pi}|\\sin(2\\pi)|=0$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":39,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=8$ and $b_n=6$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$ (so $x\\ni a_n\\cos n\\omega_0t+b_n\\sin n\\omega_0t$). Find $|c_n|$.","f":null,"o":["$7$","$2.5$","$10$","$5$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{a_n-jb_n}{2}$ ⇒ $|c_n|=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{100}=5$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":40,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±4 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_7$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$5.093$","$0.7276$","$0.1039$","$0.3638$"],"a":1,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_7=\\dfrac{4(4)}{7\\pi}=0.7276$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":41,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 4 and duty ratio 0.25 (pulse width $\\tau=0.25T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{2}|$, the magnitude of the 2th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L80.5 38.4L80.5 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L183.8 38.4L183.8 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$1$","$1.273$","$0.3183$","$0.6366$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{4}{2\\pi}|\\sin(0.5\\pi)|=0.6366$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":42,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=3$ and $b_n=4$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$ (so $x\\ni a_n\\cos n\\omega_0t+b_n\\sin n\\omega_0t$). Find $|c_n|$.","f":null,"o":["$2.5$","$3.5$","$1.25$","$5$"],"a":0,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{a_n-jb_n}{2}$ ⇒ $|c_n|=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{25}=2.5$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":43,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)=10\\cos(2t+30^\\circ)$ has exponential Fourier series $\\sum c_ke^{jk\\omega_0t}$. Find $|c_1|$.","f":null,"o":["$7.071$","$10$","$5$","$2.5$"],"a":2,"s":"$\\cos(\\omega_0t+\\phi)=\\tfrac12e^{j\\phi}e^{j\\omega_0t}+\\tfrac12e^{-j\\phi}e^{-j\\omega_0t}$ ⇒ $c_1=\\dfrac{10}{2}e^{j30^\\circ}$: $|c_1|=5$, $\\angle c_1=30^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":44,"q":"$x(t)=10\\cos(5t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{2+j\\omega}$. Find the amplitude of the output.","f":null,"o":["$1.857$","$2$","$5$","$3.714$"],"a":0,"s":"Each harmonic is scaled by $H(jk\\omega_0)$: $|H(j5)|=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt{4+25}}=0.1857$ ⇒ amplitude $1.857$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":45,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a symmetric square wave of peak value 5. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">5</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-5</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$3.183$","$0$","$5$","$2.5$"],"a":1,"s":"Equal positive and negative areas: $a_0=0$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":46,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L158.0 38.4L158.0 104.2L261.3 38.4\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)"],"a":0,"s":"The sawtooth $0\\to A$ is an odd function plus a constant $A/2$: dc term and all sine harmonics.","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":47,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)","Only sine terms, odd harmonics only"],"a":3,"s":"Odd symmetry ⇒ $a_n=0$; half-wave symmetry ⇒ only odd harmonics.","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":48,"q":"$x(t)$ has period $T=4$ s and its coefficient $c_1$ is real and positive. What is $\\angle c_1$ for $y(t)=x(t-1)$ (in degrees, principal value)?","f":null,"o":["$90^\\circ$","$180^\\circ$","$0^\\circ$","$-90^\\circ$"],"a":3,"s":"Time shift: $c_k\\to c_ke^{-jk\\omega_0t_0}$; $\\omega_0=2\\pi/4$ ⇒ angle $=-1\\cdot90^\\circ\\cdot1=-90^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":49,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 4 and duty ratio 0.25 (pulse width $\\tau=0.25T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{8}|$, the magnitude of the 8th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L80.5 38.4L80.5 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L183.8 38.4L183.8 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$1$","$2$","$0.1592$","$0$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{4}{8\\pi}|\\sin(2\\pi)|=0$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":50,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±3 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 5th. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$7.295$","$4.5$","$9$","$8.397$"],"a":3,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le5$: $8.397$ (total power $9$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":51,"q":"$x(t)=10\\cos(4t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{2+j\\omega}$. Find the amplitude of the output.","f":null,"o":["$5$","$4.472$","$2.236$","$2.5$"],"a":2,"s":"Each harmonic is scaled by $H(jk\\omega_0)$: $|H(j4)|=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt{4+16}}=0.2236$ ⇒ amplitude $2.236$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":52,"q":"$x(t)$ has period $T=4$ s and its coefficient $c_1$ is real and positive. What is $\\angle c_1$ for $y(t)=x(t-0.5)$ (in degrees, principal value)?","f":null,"o":["$-45^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$0^\\circ$","$45^\\circ$"],"a":0,"s":"Time shift: $c_k\\to c_ke^{-jk\\omega_0t_0}$; $\\omega_0=2\\pi/4$ ⇒ angle $=-1\\cdot90^\\circ\\cdot0.5=-45^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":53,"q":"A signal with half-wave symmetry $x(t+T/2)=-x(t)$ contains …","f":null,"o":["all harmonics","only even harmonics","only odd harmonics","only dc"],"a":2,"s":"Even harmonics cancel under half-wave symmetry.","m":1,"t":"Fourier series concepts"},{"i":54,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot8\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot6\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$6$","$14$","$2$","$24$"],"a":2,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(8,6)=2$ Hz (period $0.5$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":55,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot8\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot4\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$8$","$4$","$2$","$12$"],"a":1,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(8,4)=4$ Hz (period $0.25$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":56,"q":"$x(t)=2+6\\cos\\omega_0t+4\\sin\\omega_0t+3\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$112.5$","$65$","$34.5$","$8.5$"],"a":2,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=2^2+\\dfrac{6^2+4^2}{2}+\\dfrac{3^2}{2}=34.5$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":57,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)$ has period 4 s and $|c_{1}|=1$. Find $|d_{1}|$, the magnitude of the 1th coefficient of $dx/dt$.","f":null,"o":["$3.142$","$1.571$","$0.6366$","$1$"],"a":1,"s":"$dx/dt\\leftrightarrow jk\\omega_0c_k$ ⇒ $|d_1|=1\\times\\dfrac{2\\pi}{4}\\times1=1.571$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":58,"q":"A real periodic signal has exponential coefficients $c_0=1$, $|c_{\\pm1}|=1$, $|c_{\\pm2}|=1$ and all others zero. Find its average power.","f":null,"o":["$5$","$9$","$3$","$10$"],"a":0,"s":"$P=\\sum_k|c_k|^2=c_0^2+2(|c_1|^2+|c_2|^2)=1+2(1+1)=5$ (both $\\pm k$ terms count).","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":59,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)$ has period 2 s and $|c_{1}|=3$. Find $|d_{1}|$, the magnitude of the 1th coefficient of $dx/dt$.","f":null,"o":["$9.425$","$3$","$0.9549$","$18.85$"],"a":0,"s":"$dx/dt\\leftrightarrow jk\\omega_0c_k$ ⇒ $|d_1|=1\\times\\dfrac{2\\pi}{2}\\times3=9.425$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":60,"q":"The signal $x(t)=6\\cos(5t)+4\\sin(15t)$ has fundamental frequency $5$ rad/s. Find $|c_3|$ (coefficient of $e^{j15t}$).","f":null,"o":["$4$","$1$","$2$","$3$"],"a":2,"s":"$B\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{B}{2j}(e^{j\\theta}-e^{-j\\theta})$ ⇒ $|c_3|=\\dfrac{4}{2}=2$.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":61,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L158.0 38.4L158.0 104.2L261.3 38.4\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms","A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)","Only sine terms, odd harmonics only"],"a":1,"s":"The sawtooth $0\\to A$ is an odd function plus a constant $A/2$: dc term and all sine harmonics.","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":62,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a full-wave rectified sine of peak value 6. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">6</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 93.9L65.0 83.9L70.2 74.3L75.3 65.5L80.5 57.6L85.7 50.9L90.8 45.5L96.0 41.6L101.2 39.2L106.3 38.4L111.5 39.2L116.7 41.6L121.8 45.5L127.0 50.9L132.2 57.6L137.3 65.5L142.5 74.3L147.7 83.9L152.8 93.9L158.0 104.2L163.2 93.9L168.3 83.9L173.5 74.3L178.7 65.5L183.8 57.6L189.0 50.9L194.2 45.5L199.3 41.6L204.5 39.2L209.7 38.4L214.8 39.2L220.0 41.6L225.2 45.5L230.3 50.9L235.5 57.6L240.7 65.5L245.8 74.3L251.0 83.9L256.2 93.9L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$1.91$","$6$","$3$","$3.82$"],"a":3,"s":"$a_0=2A/\\pi$. $=3.82$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":63,"q":"$x(t)=0+2\\cos\\omega_0t+4\\sin\\omega_0t+3\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$29$","$4.5$","$40.5$","$14.5$"],"a":3,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=0^2+\\dfrac{2^2+4^2}{2}+\\dfrac{3^2}{2}=14.5$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":64,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a sawtooth rising from 0 to A of peak value 4. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L158.0 38.4L158.0 104.2L261.3 38.4\"/></svg>","o":["$2.546$","$1.273$","$4$","$2$"],"a":3,"s":"Linear ramp from 0 to $A$: average $A/2$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":65,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L158.0 38.4L158.0 104.2L261.3 38.4\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","Only sine terms, odd harmonics only","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)"],"a":0,"s":"The sawtooth $0\\to A$ is an odd function plus a constant $A/2$: dc term and all sine harmonics.","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":66,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 93.9L65.0 83.9L70.2 74.3L75.3 65.5L80.5 57.6L85.7 50.9L90.8 45.5L96.0 41.6L101.2 39.2L106.3 38.4L111.5 39.2L116.7 41.6L121.8 45.5L127.0 50.9L132.2 57.6L137.3 65.5L142.5 74.3L147.7 83.9L152.8 93.9L158.0 104.2L163.2 93.9L168.3 83.9L173.5 74.3L178.7 65.5L183.8 57.6L189.0 50.9L194.2 45.5L199.3 41.6L204.5 39.2L209.7 38.4L214.8 39.2L220.0 41.6L225.2 45.5L230.3 50.9L235.5 57.6L240.7 65.5L245.8 74.3L251.0 83.9L256.2 93.9L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["Only sine terms, odd harmonics only","A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)"],"a":2,"s":"$|\\sin|$ is an even function ($x(-t)=x(t)$), so $b_n=0$; its average is non-zero and the cosine harmonics $\\cos(2\\pi kt/T)$ of all orders appear (coefficients $\\propto 1/(4k^2-1)$).","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":67,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a symmetric triangular wave of peak value 2. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-2</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 70.1L80.5 28.6L132.2 111.6L183.8 28.6L235.5 111.6L261.3 70.1\"/></svg>","o":["$1.273$","$0$","$1$","$2$"],"a":1,"s":"Symmetric about zero: positive and negative areas cancel, $a_0=0$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":68,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 83.9L65.0 65.5L70.2 50.9L75.3 41.6L80.5 38.4L85.7 41.6L90.8 50.9L96.0 65.5L101.2 83.9L106.3 104.2L111.5 104.2L116.7 104.2L121.8 104.2L127.0 104.2L132.2 104.2L137.3 104.2L142.5 104.2L147.7 104.2L152.8 104.2L158.0 104.2L163.2 83.9L168.3 65.5L173.5 50.9L178.7 41.6L183.8 38.4L189.0 41.6L194.2 50.9L199.3 65.5L204.5 83.9L209.7 104.2L214.8 104.2L220.0 104.2L225.2 104.2L230.3 104.2L235.5 104.2L240.7 104.2L245.8 104.2L251.0 104.2L256.2 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms","Only sine terms, odd harmonics only"],"a":2,"s":"Half-wave rectified sine contains dc, the fundamental sine, and even harmonics only (no odd harmonics except the fundamental).","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":69,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 5 and duty ratio 0.5 (pulse width $\\tau=0.5T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{2}|$, the magnitude of the 2th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">5</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L106.3 38.4L106.3 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L209.7 38.4L209.7 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$0$","$2.5$","$1$","$0.7958$"],"a":0,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{5}{2\\pi}|\\sin(1\\pi)|=0$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":70,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±1 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 3rd. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$0.5$","$0.8106$","$1$","$0.9006$"],"a":3,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le3$: $0.9006$ (total power $1$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":71,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)$ has period 4 s and $|c_{2}|=2$. Find $|d_{2}|$, the magnitude of the 2th coefficient of $dx/dt$.","f":null,"o":["$3.142$","$6.283$","$2$","$4$"],"a":1,"s":"$dx/dt\\leftrightarrow jk\\omega_0c_k$ ⇒ $|d_2|=2\\times\\dfrac{2\\pi}{4}\\times2=6.283$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":72,"q":"Find $c_0$ of $x(t)=2+10\\cos(5t)+1\\sin(15t)$.","f":null,"o":["$1$","$5$","$12$","$2$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_0$ is the average value (DC term) $=2$; the sinusoids average to zero.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":73,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot20\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot6\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$2$","$60$","$6$","$26$"],"a":0,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(20,6)=2$ Hz (period $0.5$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":74,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±2 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_9$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-2</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$2.546$","$0.03144$","$0.2829$","$0.1415$"],"a":2,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_9=\\dfrac{4(2)}{9\\pi}=0.2829$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":75,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±4 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 5th. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$16$","$8$","$12.97$","$14.93$"],"a":3,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le5$: $14.93$ (total power $16$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":76,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)$ has period 2 s and $|c_{4}|=4$. Find $|d_{4}|$, the magnitude of the 4th coefficient of $dx/dt$.","f":null,"o":["$12.57$","$50.27$","$4$","$16$"],"a":1,"s":"$dx/dt\\leftrightarrow jk\\omega_0c_k$ ⇒ $|d_4|=4\\times\\dfrac{2\\pi}{2}\\times4=50.27$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":77,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±3 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_2$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$0.9549$","$0$","$3.82$","$1.5$"],"a":1,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $n=2$ is even ⇒ $b_2=0$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":78,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±1 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 1st. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$1$","$0.5$","$0.4053$","$0.8106$"],"a":3,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le1$: $0.8106$ (total power $1$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":79,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 70.1L80.5 28.6L132.2 111.6L183.8 28.6L235.5 111.6L261.3 70.1\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)","Only sine terms, odd harmonics only"],"a":3,"s":"The wave (as drawn, starting at 0 going up) is odd with half-wave symmetry: only odd-harmonic sine terms.","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":80,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a sawtooth rising from 0 to A of peak value 6. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">6</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L158.0 38.4L158.0 104.2L261.3 38.4\"/></svg>","o":["$3$","$6$","$3.82$","$2.4$"],"a":0,"s":"Linear ramp from 0 to $A$: average $A/2$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":81,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±3 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 1st. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$7.295$","$3.648$","$9$","$4.5$"],"a":0,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le1$: $7.295$ (total power $9$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":82,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=2$ and $b_n=2$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$ (so $x\\ni a_n\\cos n\\omega_0t+b_n\\sin n\\omega_0t$). Find $|c_n|$.","f":null,"o":["$0.7071$","$1.414$","$2$","$2.828$"],"a":1,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{a_n-jb_n}{2}$ ⇒ $|c_n|=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{8}=1.414$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":83,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a rectangular pulse train (high for a fraction 0.2 of the period) of peak value 6. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">6</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L75.3 38.4L75.3 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L178.7 38.4L178.7 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$6$","$3.82$","$1.2$","$3$"],"a":2,"s":"$a_0=A\\,D=6\\times0.2=1.2$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":84,"q":"$x(t)=0+2\\cos\\omega_0t+3\\sin\\omega_0t+1\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$3$","$14$","$18$","$7$"],"a":3,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=0^2+\\dfrac{2^2+3^2}{2}+\\dfrac{1^2}{2}=7$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":85,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 4 and duty ratio 0.5 (pulse width $\\tau=0.5T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{5}|$, the magnitude of the 5th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L106.3 38.4L106.3 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L209.7 38.4L209.7 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$0.5093$","$1.273$","$2$","$0.2546$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{4}{5\\pi}|\\sin(2.5\\pi)|=0.2546$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":86,"q":"The signal $x(t)=2\\cos(1t)+3\\sin(3t)$ has fundamental frequency $1$ rad/s. Find $|c_3|$ (coefficient of $e^{j3t}$).","f":null,"o":["$1.5$","$0.75$","$1$","$3$"],"a":0,"s":"$B\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{B}{2j}(e^{j\\theta}-e^{-j\\theta})$ ⇒ $|c_3|=\\dfrac{3}{2}=1.5$.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":87,"q":"$x(t)=2+2\\cos\\omega_0t+3\\sin\\omega_0t+2\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$21$","$5.5$","$12.5$","$40.5$"],"a":2,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=2^2+\\dfrac{2^2+3^2}{2}+\\dfrac{2^2}{2}=12.5$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":88,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±1 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_3$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">1</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-1</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$0.2122$","$1.273$","$0.4244$","$0.1415$"],"a":2,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_3=\\dfrac{4(1)}{3\\pi}=0.4244$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":89,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot10\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot3\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$13$","$30$","$3$","$1$"],"a":3,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(10,3)=1$ Hz (period $1$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":90,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=1$ and $b_n=1$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$. Find $\\angle c_n$ in degrees.","f":null,"o":["$135^\\circ$","$45^\\circ$","$-90^\\circ$","$-45^\\circ$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{1-j1}{2}$ ⇒ $\\angle c_n=-\\tan^{-1}(b_n/a_n)=-45^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":91,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±2 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_5$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-2</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$2.546$","$0.5093$","$0.2546$","$0.1019$"],"a":1,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_5=\\dfrac{4(2)}{5\\pi}=0.5093$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":92,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 93.9L65.0 83.9L70.2 74.3L75.3 65.5L80.5 57.6L85.7 50.9L90.8 45.5L96.0 41.6L101.2 39.2L106.3 38.4L111.5 39.2L116.7 41.6L121.8 45.5L127.0 50.9L132.2 57.6L137.3 65.5L142.5 74.3L147.7 83.9L152.8 93.9L158.0 104.2L163.2 93.9L168.3 83.9L173.5 74.3L178.7 65.5L183.8 57.6L189.0 50.9L194.2 45.5L199.3 41.6L204.5 39.2L209.7 38.4L214.8 39.2L220.0 41.6L225.2 45.5L230.3 50.9L235.5 57.6L240.7 65.5L245.8 74.3L251.0 83.9L256.2 93.9L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms","Only sine terms, odd harmonics only"],"a":0,"s":"$|\\sin|$ is an even function ($x(-t)=x(t)$), so $b_n=0$; its average is non-zero and the cosine harmonics $\\cos(2\\pi kt/T)$ of all orders appear (coefficients $\\propto 1/(4k^2-1)$).","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":93,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=5$ and $b_n=12$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$ (so $x\\ni a_n\\cos n\\omega_0t+b_n\\sin n\\omega_0t$). Find $|c_n|$.","f":null,"o":["$6.5$","$13$","$8.5$","$3.25$"],"a":0,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{a_n-jb_n}{2}$ ⇒ $|c_n|=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{169}=6.5$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":94,"q":"$x(t)=2+6\\cos\\omega_0t+3\\sin\\omega_0t+2\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$7.5$","$28.5$","$53$","$84.5$"],"a":1,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=2^2+\\dfrac{6^2+3^2}{2}+\\dfrac{2^2}{2}=28.5$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":95,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot3\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot6\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$1.5$","$3$","$9$","$6$"],"a":1,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(3,6)=3$ Hz (period $0.3333$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":96,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot6\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot15\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$3$","$21$","$30$","$6$"],"a":0,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(6,15)=3$ Hz (period $0.3333$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":97,"q":"$x(t)=3+2\\cos(2t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{1+j\\omega}$. Find the dc component of the output.","f":null,"o":["$6$","$3$","$1.5$","$5$"],"a":1,"s":"DC passes through $H(0)=1/1$: output dc $=3/1=3$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":98,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a symmetric triangular wave of peak value 4. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 70.1L80.5 28.6L132.2 111.6L183.8 28.6L235.5 111.6L261.3 70.1\"/></svg>","o":["$4$","$0$","$2$","$2.546$"],"a":1,"s":"Symmetric about zero: positive and negative areas cancel, $a_0=0$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":99,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=10$ and $b_n=24$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$ (so $x\\ni a_n\\cos n\\omega_0t+b_n\\sin n\\omega_0t$). Find $|c_n|$.","f":null,"o":["$6.5$","$13$","$17$","$26$"],"a":1,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{a_n-jb_n}{2}$ ⇒ $|c_n|=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{a_n^2+b_n^2}=\\dfrac12\\sqrt{676}=13$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":100,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a sawtooth rising from 0 to A of peak value 3. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L158.0 38.4L158.0 104.2L261.3 38.4\"/></svg>","o":["$0.9549$","$3$","$1.91$","$1.5$"],"a":3,"s":"Linear ramp from 0 to $A$: average $A/2$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":101,"q":"$x(t)$ has period $T=4$ s and its coefficient $c_3$ is real and positive. What is $\\angle c_3$ for $y(t)=x(t-0.25)$ (in degrees, principal value)?","f":null,"o":["$-67.5^\\circ$","$67.5^\\circ$","$0^\\circ$","$135^\\circ$"],"a":0,"s":"Time shift: $c_k\\to c_ke^{-jk\\omega_0t_0}$; $\\omega_0=2\\pi/4$ ⇒ angle $=-3\\cdot90^\\circ\\cdot0.25=-67.5^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":102,"q":"The periodic waveform shown is a half-wave rectified sine of peak value 2. Find the coefficient $a_0$ (average value).","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 83.9L65.0 65.5L70.2 50.9L75.3 41.6L80.5 38.4L85.7 41.6L90.8 50.9L96.0 65.5L101.2 83.9L106.3 104.2L111.5 104.2L116.7 104.2L121.8 104.2L127.0 104.2L132.2 104.2L137.3 104.2L142.5 104.2L147.7 104.2L152.8 104.2L158.0 104.2L163.2 83.9L168.3 65.5L173.5 50.9L178.7 41.6L183.8 38.4L189.0 41.6L194.2 50.9L199.3 65.5L204.5 83.9L209.7 104.2L214.8 104.2L220.0 104.2L225.2 104.2L230.3 104.2L235.5 104.2L240.7 104.2L245.8 104.2L251.0 104.2L256.2 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$0.6366$","$2$","$1.273$","$1$"],"a":0,"s":"$a_0=A/\\pi$. $=0.6366$.","m":2,"t":"Average value (DC coefficient) from the waveform"},{"i":103,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±4 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_9$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$0.06288$","$5.093$","$0.5659$","$0.2829$"],"a":2,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_9=\\dfrac{4(4)}{9\\pi}=0.5659$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":104,"q":"$x(t)=4\\cos(4t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{3+j\\omega}$. Find the amplitude of the output.","f":null,"o":["$1$","$0.8$","$1.6$","$1.333$"],"a":1,"s":"Each harmonic is scaled by $H(jk\\omega_0)$: $|H(j4)|=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt{9+16}}=0.2$ ⇒ amplitude $0.8$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":105,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)=10\\cos(2t+45^\\circ)$ has exponential Fourier series $\\sum c_ke^{jk\\omega_0t}$. Find $|c_1|$.","f":null,"o":["$2.5$","$7.071$","$10$","$5$"],"a":3,"s":"$\\cos(\\omega_0t+\\phi)=\\tfrac12e^{j\\phi}e^{j\\omega_0t}+\\tfrac12e^{-j\\phi}e^{-j\\omega_0t}$ ⇒ $c_1=\\dfrac{10}{2}e^{j45^\\circ}$: $|c_1|=5$, $\\angle c_1=45^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":106,"q":"$x(t)=2+2\\cos\\omega_0t+4\\sin\\omega_0t+1\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$5.5$","$14.5$","$25$","$40.5$"],"a":1,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=2^2+\\dfrac{2^2+4^2}{2}+\\dfrac{1^2}{2}=14.5$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":107,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["Only sine terms, odd harmonics only","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)","A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms"],"a":0,"s":"Odd symmetry ⇒ $a_n=0$; half-wave symmetry ⇒ only odd harmonics.","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":108,"q":"$x(t)=2+5\\cos(2t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{3+j\\omega}$. Find the dc component of the output.","f":null,"o":["$0.6667$","$2$","$6$","$0.2222$"],"a":0,"s":"DC passes through $H(0)=1/3$: output dc $=2/3=0.6667$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":109,"q":"For an even periodic signal, the trigonometric Fourier series contains …","f":null,"o":["only sine terms","only the fundamental","only odd harmonics","only dc and cosine terms"],"a":3,"s":"$b_n=\\frac{2}{T}\\int x(t)\\sin(n\\omega_0t)dt=0$ for even $x$.","m":1,"t":"Fourier series concepts"},{"i":110,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=6$ and $b_n=8$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$. Find $\\angle c_n$ in degrees.","f":null,"o":["$-53.13^\\circ$","$36.87^\\circ$","$143.1^\\circ$","$53.13^\\circ$"],"a":0,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{6-j8}{2}$ ⇒ $\\angle c_n=-\\tan^{-1}(b_n/a_n)=-53.13^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":111,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 2 and duty ratio 0.2 (pulse width $\\tau=0.2T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{8}|$, the magnitude of the 8th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L75.3 38.4L75.3 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L178.7 38.4L178.7 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$0.4$","$0.07568$","$0.07958$","$-0.6055$"],"a":1,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{2}{8\\pi}|\\sin(1.6\\pi)|=0.07568$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":112,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot10\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot6\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$30$","$16$","$2$","$6$"],"a":2,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(10,6)=2$ Hz (period $0.5$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":113,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot10\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot4\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$20$","$4$","$14$","$2$"],"a":3,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(10,4)=2$ Hz (period $0.5$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":114,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±3 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_9$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$3.82$","$0.4244$","$0.2122$","$0.04716$"],"a":1,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_9=\\dfrac{4(3)}{9\\pi}=0.4244$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":115,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)$ has period 4 s and $|c_{1}|=3$. Find $|d_{1}|$, the magnitude of the 1th coefficient of $dx/dt$.","f":null,"o":["$4.712$","$1.91$","$3$","$9.425$"],"a":0,"s":"$dx/dt\\leftrightarrow jk\\omega_0c_k$ ⇒ $|d_1|=1\\times\\dfrac{2\\pi}{4}\\times3=4.712$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":116,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L59.8 83.9L65.0 65.5L70.2 50.9L75.3 41.6L80.5 38.4L85.7 41.6L90.8 50.9L96.0 65.5L101.2 83.9L106.3 104.2L111.5 104.2L116.7 104.2L121.8 104.2L127.0 104.2L132.2 104.2L137.3 104.2L142.5 104.2L147.7 104.2L152.8 104.2L158.0 104.2L163.2 83.9L168.3 65.5L173.5 50.9L178.7 41.6L183.8 38.4L189.0 41.6L194.2 50.9L199.3 65.5L204.5 83.9L209.7 104.2L214.8 104.2L220.0 104.2L225.2 104.2L230.3 104.2L235.5 104.2L240.7 104.2L245.8 104.2L251.0 104.2L256.2 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["A dc term, the fundamental sine, and even-harmonic cosine terms","A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics"],"a":0,"s":"Half-wave rectified sine contains dc, the fundamental sine, and even harmonics only (no odd harmonics except the fundamental).","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":117,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot12\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot3\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$6$","$12$","$3$","$15$"],"a":2,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(12,3)=3$ Hz (period $0.3333$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":118,"q":"$x(t)=4\\cos(5t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{4+j\\omega}$. Find the amplitude of the output.","f":null,"o":["$1$","$0.6247$","$1.249$","$0.8$"],"a":1,"s":"Each harmonic is scaled by $H(jk\\omega_0)$: $|H(j5)|=\\dfrac1{\\sqrt{16+25}}=0.1562$ ⇒ amplitude $0.6247$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":119,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)$ has period 2 s and $|c_{3}|=4$. Find $|d_{3}|$, the magnitude of the 3th coefficient of $dx/dt$.","f":null,"o":["$37.7$","$12$","$12.57$","$4$"],"a":0,"s":"$dx/dt\\leftrightarrow jk\\omega_0c_k$ ⇒ $|d_3|=3\\times\\dfrac{2\\pi}{2}\\times4=37.7$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":120,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±4 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 1st. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$8$","$12.97$","$16$","$6.485$"],"a":1,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le1$: $12.97$ (total power $16$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":121,"q":"At a point of discontinuity the Fourier series converges to …","f":null,"o":["the right limit","the left limit","the average of the left and right limits","zero"],"a":2,"s":"Dirichlet theorem.","m":1,"t":"Fourier series concepts"},{"i":122,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)$ has period 2 s and $|c_{2}|=3$. Find $|d_{2}|$, the magnitude of the 2th coefficient of $dx/dt$.","f":null,"o":["$9.425$","$3$","$18.85$","$6$"],"a":2,"s":"$dx/dt\\leftrightarrow jk\\omega_0c_k$ ⇒ $|d_2|=2\\times\\dfrac{2\\pi}{2}\\times3=18.85$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":123,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 5 and duty ratio 0.1 (pulse width $\\tau=0.1T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{4}|$, the magnitude of the 4th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">5</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L65.0 38.4L65.0 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L168.3 38.4L168.3 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$0.3979$","$0.5$","$1.514$","$0.3784$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{5}{4\\pi}|\\sin(0.4\\pi)|=0.3784$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":124,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 2 and duty ratio 0.5 (pulse width $\\tau=0.5T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{1}|$, the magnitude of the 1th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">2</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L106.3 38.4L106.3 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L209.7 38.4L209.7 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$1$","$0.3183$","$1.273$","$0.6366$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{2}{1\\pi}|\\sin(0.5\\pi)|=0.6366$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":125,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot2\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot9\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$2$","$18$","$11$","$1$"],"a":3,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(2,9)=1$ Hz (period $1$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":126,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot8\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot3\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$3$","$1$","$24$","$11$"],"a":1,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(8,3)=1$ Hz (period $1$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":127,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±3 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_3$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$0.6366$","$1.273$","$3.82$","$0.4244$"],"a":1,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_3=\\dfrac{4(3)}{3\\pi}=1.273$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":128,"q":"A real periodic signal has exponential coefficients $c_0=3$, $|c_{\\pm1}|=3$, $|c_{\\pm2}|=2$ and all others zero. Find its average power.","f":null,"o":["$64$","$70$","$22$","$35$"],"a":3,"s":"$P=\\sum_k|c_k|^2=c_0^2+2(|c_1|^2+|c_2|^2)=9+2(9+4)=35$ (both $\\pm k$ terms count).","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":129,"q":"Find $c_0$ of $x(t)=2+8\\cos(1t)+4\\sin(3t)$.","f":null,"o":["$4$","$1$","$2$","$10$"],"a":2,"s":"$c_0$ is the average value (DC term) $=2$; the sinusoids average to zero.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":130,"q":"$x(t)=2+10\\cos(1t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{1+j\\omega}$. Find the dc component of the output.","f":null,"o":["$4$","$12$","$2$","$1$"],"a":2,"s":"DC passes through $H(0)=1/1$: output dc $=2/1=2$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":131,"q":"$x(t)=1+2\\cos\\omega_0t+2\\sin\\omega_0t+3\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$9.5$","$18$","$4.5$","$32$"],"a":0,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=1^2+\\dfrac{2^2+2^2}{2}+\\dfrac{3^2}{2}=9.5$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":132,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)$ has period 4 s and $|c_{3}|=2$. Find $|d_{3}|$, the magnitude of the 3th coefficient of $dx/dt$.","f":null,"o":["$9.425$","$6$","$2$","$3.142$"],"a":0,"s":"$dx/dt\\leftrightarrow jk\\omega_0c_k$ ⇒ $|d_3|=3\\times\\dfrac{2\\pi}{4}\\times2=9.425$.","m":2,"t":"Time shift and differentiation properties"},{"i":133,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±5 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 1st. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$25$","$20.26$","$12.5$","$10.13$"],"a":1,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le1$: $20.26$ (total power $25$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":134,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)=6\\cos(5t+0^\\circ)$ has exponential Fourier series $\\sum c_ke^{jk\\omega_0t}$. Find $\\angle c_1$ in degrees.","f":null,"o":["$0^\\circ$","$15^\\circ$","$90^\\circ$","$1^\\circ$"],"a":0,"s":"$\\cos(\\omega_0t+\\phi)=\\tfrac12e^{j\\phi}e^{j\\omega_0t}+\\tfrac12e^{-j\\phi}e^{-j\\omega_0t}$ ⇒ $c_1=\\dfrac{6}{2}e^{j0^\\circ}$: $|c_1|=3$, $\\angle c_1=0^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":135,"q":"Parseval's theorem for a periodic signal states …","f":null,"o":["$P=|c_0|$","$\\dfrac1T\\int x\\,dt=\\sum|c_k|$","$\\dfrac1T\\int_T|x|^2dt=\\sum|c_k|^2$","$\\int|x|^2dt=\\sum c_k$"],"a":2,"s":"Power in time equals power in frequency.","m":1,"t":"Fourier series concepts"},{"i":136,"q":"Find the fundamental frequency (Hz) of $x(t)=\\cos(2\\pi\\cdot3\\,t)+\\sin(2\\pi\\cdot5\\,t)$.","f":null,"o":["$15$","$3$","$1$","$8$"],"a":2,"s":"The fundamental frequency is the greatest common divisor of the component frequencies: $\\gcd(3,5)=1$ Hz (period $1$ s).","m":2,"t":"Fundamental frequency"},{"i":137,"q":"$x(t)=4+10\\cos(1t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{2+j\\omega}$. Find the dc component of the output.","f":null,"o":["$2$","$8$","$4$","$1$"],"a":0,"s":"DC passes through $H(0)=1/2$: output dc $=4/2=2$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":138,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±2 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 5th. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$2$","$3.242$","$4$","$3.732$"],"a":3,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le5$: $3.732$ (total power $4$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"},{"i":139,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±1 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_1$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">1</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-1</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$1.273$","$0.6366$","$2.546$","$1$"],"a":0,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_1=\\dfrac{4(1)}{1\\pi}=1.273$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":140,"q":"The pulse train shown has amplitude 4 and duty ratio 0.25 (pulse width $\\tau=0.25T$, starting at $t=0$). Find $|c_{5}|$, the magnitude of the 5th exponential coefficient.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">4</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L80.5 38.4L80.5 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L183.8 38.4L183.8 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["$-0.9003$","$0.2546$","$0.1801$","$1$"],"a":2,"s":"$c_k=\\dfrac{A\\tau}{T}\\,\\mathrm{sinc}(k\\tau/T)e^{-jk\\pi\\tau/T}$ ⇒ $|c_k|=\\dfrac{A}{k\\pi}\\left|\\sin(k\\pi D)\\right|=\\dfrac{4}{5\\pi}|\\sin(1.25\\pi)|=0.1801$.","m":2,"t":"Pulse-train coefficients"},{"i":141,"q":"A real periodic signal has exponential coefficients $c_0=1$, $|c_{\\pm1}|=2$, $|c_{\\pm2}|=1$ and all others zero. Find its average power.","f":null,"o":["$22$","$6$","$11$","$16$"],"a":2,"s":"$P=\\sum_k|c_k|^2=c_0^2+2(|c_1|^2+|c_2|^2)=1+2(4+1)=11$ (both $\\pm k$ terms count).","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":142,"q":"A real periodic signal has exponential coefficients $c_0=3$, $|c_{\\pm1}|=3$, $|c_{\\pm2}|=1$ and all others zero. Find its average power.","f":null,"o":["$49$","$29$","$19$","$58$"],"a":1,"s":"$P=\\sum_k|c_k|^2=c_0^2+2(|c_1|^2+|c_2|^2)=9+2(9+1)=29$ (both $\\pm k$ terms count).","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":143,"q":"The odd square wave of amplitude ±10 shown (positive for the first half-period) is written as $x(t)=\\sum b_n\\sin(n\\omega_0t)$. Find $b_7$.","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 70.1L288.0 70.1\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 70.1L282.5 72.4L282.5 67.7Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 67.1L158.0 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 67.1L261.3 73.1\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"88.1\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 28.6L57.7 28.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"32.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 111.6L57.7 111.6\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"115.6\" text-anchor=\"end\">-10</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"64.1\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 28.6L106.3 28.6L106.3 111.6L158.0 111.6L158.0 28.6L209.7 28.6L209.7 111.6L261.3 111.6\"/></svg>","o":["$0.9095$","$0.2598$","$12.73$","$1.819$"],"a":3,"s":"For this odd, half-wave-symmetric wave, $b_n=\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}$ for odd $n$ and $0$ for even $n$. $b_7=\\dfrac{4(10)}{7\\pi}=1.819$.","m":2,"t":"Fourier coefficients of a square wave"},{"i":144,"q":"$x(t)=2+4\\cos\\omega_0t+3\\sin\\omega_0t+1\\cos2\\omega_0t$. Find the average power.","f":null,"o":["$17$","$30$","$6$","$50$"],"a":0,"s":"$P=a_0^2+\\sum\\dfrac{a_n^2+b_n^2}{2}=2^2+\\dfrac{4^2+3^2}{2}+\\dfrac{1^2}{2}=17$.","m":2,"t":"Parseval's theorem (power)"},{"i":145,"q":"The periodic signal $x(t)=4\\cos(10t+0^\\circ)$ has exponential Fourier series $\\sum c_ke^{jk\\omega_0t}$. Find $|c_1|$.","f":null,"o":["$1$","$2.828$","$2$","$4$"],"a":2,"s":"$\\cos(\\omega_0t+\\phi)=\\tfrac12e^{j\\phi}e^{j\\omega_0t}+\\tfrac12e^{-j\\phi}e^{-j\\omega_0t}$ ⇒ $c_1=\\dfrac{4}{2}e^{j0^\\circ}$: $|c_1|=2$, $\\angle c_1=0^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":146,"q":"$x(t)=4+2\\cos(3t)$ is the input to a system $H(j\\omega)=\\dfrac{1}{3+j\\omega}$. Find the dc component of the output.","f":null,"o":["$0.4444$","$1.333$","$12$","$4$"],"a":1,"s":"DC passes through $H(0)=1/3$: output dc $=4/3=1.333$.","m":2,"t":"Periodic input to an LTI system"},{"i":147,"q":"A real periodic signal has $a_n=3$ and $b_n=4$ at some harmonic $n\\ge1$. Find $\\angle c_n$ in degrees.","f":null,"o":["$36.87^\\circ$","$143.1^\\circ$","$53.13^\\circ$","$-53.13^\\circ$"],"a":3,"s":"$c_n=\\dfrac{3-j4}{2}$ ⇒ $\\angle c_n=-\\tan^{-1}(b_n/a_n)=-53.13^\\circ$.","m":2,"t":"Relations between a_n, b_n and c_n"},{"i":148,"q":"Which description of the trigonometric Fourier series of the waveform shown is correct?","f":"<svg class=\"fg\" viewBox=\"0 0 300 150\" width=\"360\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path class=\"w\" d=\"M30.0 104.2L288.0 104.2\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M288.0 104.2L282.5 106.6L282.5 101.9Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M54.7 128.0L54.7 6.0\"/><path class=\"f\" d=\"M54.7 6.0L57.0 11.5L52.3 11.5Z\"/><path class=\"w\" d=\"M158.0 101.2L158.0 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"158.0\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M261.3 101.2L261.3 107.2\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"261.3\" y=\"122.2\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2T</text><path class=\"w\" d=\"M51.7 38.4L57.7 38.4\"/><text class=\"t\" x=\"48.7\" y=\"42.4\" text-anchor=\"end\">3</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"284.0\" y=\"98.2\" text-anchor=\"end\">t</text><text class=\"t\" x=\"60.7\" y=\"10.0\" text-anchor=\"start\">x(t)</text><path class=\"a\" d=\"M54.7 104.2L54.7 38.4L80.5 38.4L80.5 104.2L158.0 104.2L158.0 38.4L183.8 38.4L183.8 104.2L261.3 104.2\"/></svg>","o":["Only sine terms, odd harmonics only","A dc term and sine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and cosine terms of all harmonics","A dc term and a mix of cosine and sine terms (pulse starts at $t=0$)"],"a":3,"s":"A pulse starting at $t=0$ is neither even nor odd, so both $a_n$ and $b_n$ are present.","m":2,"t":"Symmetry and harmonics present"},{"i":149,"q":"The signal $x(t)=8\\cos(1t)+2\\sin(3t)$ has fundamental frequency $1$ rad/s. Find $|c_3|$ (coefficient of $e^{j3t}$).","f":null,"o":["$2$","$0.5$","$4$","$1$"],"a":3,"s":"$B\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{B}{2j}(e^{j\\theta}-e^{-j\\theta})$ ⇒ $|c_3|=\\dfrac{2}{2}=1$.","m":2,"t":"Exponential coefficients of sinusoids"},{"i":150,"q":"A symmetric square wave of amplitude ±1 is passed through an ideal filter that keeps only the harmonics up to the 5th. Find the average power of the output.","f":null,"o":["$0.8106$","$0.5$","$0.9331$","$1$"],"a":2,"s":"$P_n=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\left(\\dfrac{4A}{n\\pi}\\right)^2=\\dfrac{8A^2}{n^2\\pi^2}$ (odd $n$). Sum over odd $n\\le5$: $0.9331$ (total power $1$).","m":2,"t":"Power in the fundamental of a square wave"}]};